Z||000000||Hawkman||05-01-2000||08:33 AM||||My '85 4 cylinder engine is having some problems  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif">)<P>It idles rough (tach hunting) and has an evident miss.  Starting it cold (after sitting all night) produces a blue cloud. The gas mileage is still good at 34 and the oil pressure is howing about 60+ most of the time. I have not done a compression test yet.<P>I replaced the cap, rotor, wires, plugs,PVC valve, and air cleaner over the weekend.  Unfortunately the "tune-up" did not make it run any better. The old plugs looked normal - light brown with no deposits or signs of problems. I have ordered a new idle air control valve, O2 sensor, and air cleaner temperature sensor.<P>So with my limited engine knowledge...<BR>I'm pretty sure that the valve seals have gone bad and is causing the cold start smoke. I could have a bad valve or two that could be causing the miss or I have some kind of fuel delivery problem. Okay so I'm guessing ...<P>Should I just "bite the bullet" and just replace the entire head with a rebuilt one? If so, can you recommend a good remanfactured head source?<P>Please help!!!<P>Thanks!||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||05-01-2000||11:04 AM||||air cleaner temp sensor? all that does is open the thermac door. either works or it doesn't. likely won't cause problems you describe..<P>Yup. likely valve stems casuing the smoke.<P>If you replace the head buy NEW head bolts. Don't reuse the old ones.<P>I'd check for vacuum leaks. especially the TBI base the brake boster line and the PCV valve line. If it's hunting I doubt the IAC motor is bad. It's likely the IAC & TBI aren't the only path for air entering the engine.<P>check ECM coolant sensor. the older ones are prone to cruddy connections. that will cause problems.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 05-01-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||AL||05-01-2000||09:17 PM||||WHY BUY? when you can take it to a good shop and have them recondition it,but if you have money, what the heck go for it.||||reg||1
